OverlayController:
```kotlin
private var lastShowAt = 0L   // show() : lastShowAt = SystemClock.uptimeMillis()
inner class OverlayBridge(private val owner: WebView) {
    @JavascriptInterface
    fun rects(json: String) { Hub.main.post { if (web === owner) syncHandles(json) } }
    // Plus aucun drop visuel : WebView libérée 20 s plus tard (marge pour un
    // TTS qui finit après l'image) au lieu de 90 s.
    @JavascriptInterface
    fun idle() { Hub.main.post {
        if (web === owner && SystemClock.uptimeMillis() - lastShowAt > 2_000) {
            Hub.main.removeCallbacks(idleRemove)
            Hub.main.postDelayed(idleRemove, 20_000L)
        }
    } }
}
// ensureView : w.addJavascriptInterface(OverlayBridge(w), "MDOverlay")
```
Keep the 90 s timer armed in show() as a fallback: TTS-only and rain-only drops never take a slot, so they never trigger stageEmpty. The owner check also discards stale rects posted by a WebView that has already been destroyed.

```kotlin
private var lastRxAt = 0L   // onSocketMessage() : lastRxAt = SystemClock.elapsedRealtime()
// Réseau revenu / écran rallumé : on n'attend ni la fin du backoff ni le
// heartbeat (timers Handler gelés pendant la veille profonde).
private fun kick() {
    if (Prefs.paused) return
    val open = Hub.status == "linked" || Hub.status == "awaiting_link"
    if (ws == null || (open && SystemClock.elapsedRealtime() - lastRxAt > HEARTBEAT_TIMEOUT_MS)) {
        attempts = 0
        connect()
    }
}
private val netCallback = object : ConnectivityManager.NetworkCallback() {
    override fun onAvailable(network: Network) { Hub.main.post { kick() } }
}
```
onCreate: runCatching { getSystemService(ConnectivityManager::class.java).registerDefaultNetworkCallback(netCallback) }; onDestroy: runCatching { ...unregisterNetworkCallback(netCallback) }. Call kick() on ACTION_SCREEN_ON (from the receiver shared with the locked-drops finding, or its own). Manifest: <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE" />. Jitter (l.156): multiply the computed delay by (0.8 + Math.random() * 0.4).

